<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hindu-Buddhist</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hindu-Buddhist refers to the blended religious and cultural tradition, drawing on both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hinduism</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>, that shaped many states of South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a> was its last great expression in the Indonesian archipelago. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> spread through the region, Hindu-Buddhist culture retreated, surviving most notably in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>.</p></div>
